From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:59:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 27/40] Remember the window size and maximized state across
 restarts

The session now keeps the main window's size in logical pixels and
whether it was maximized. With "Restore previous session" on, the
window opens at that size (clamped to 360x240..8192x8192) and is
maximized again if it was. A maximized window keeps the size it had
before, so unmaximizing returns to it. Position is not kept: a Wayland
client cannot place its window. Old sessions without the field load
with the default size; an editor that does not own the session does not
save its size.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

